WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.200
<b>Sabo's Sea</b>

3
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.440
It's all over, isn't it?

4
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.610
It's too late
to put out the fire, Captain!

5
00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.040
We gotta abandon the ship!

6
00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.150
The sea is blocked off anyway!

7
00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.420
Damn the king!

8
00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.150
That filthy cheat thinks
he can get away with this?

9
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:03.490
Just you wait. You're dead!

10
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:11.480
Must Gray Terminal be an assault to my
senses, even in its final moments?

11
00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.850
That light is far too bright!

12
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.480
We are sorry, your majesty.

13
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.880
Please allow us to close the curtains.

14
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:27.270
Say, Papa, how come we wanna
burn everybody in Gray Terminal?

15
00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.040
Aren't they people too, just like us?

16
00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.770
Not exactly.

17
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.070
They chose to live meaningless lives.

18
00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.670
Just think about it.

19
00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.340
If they had chosen the
path of high-class nobility

20
00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.480
like you and me,
they wouldn't be in this mess.

21
00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.300
They wouldn't?

22
00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.280
I get it!

23
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.210
You mean it's their fault for
being born all poor and dumb!

24
00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.410
How silly!

25
00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.340
Yes.

26
00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.980
Now enough about those people.

27
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.780
You need to get some
studying done before bedtime.

28
00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.150
M'kay!

29
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.280
See you tomorrow.

30
00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.260
Hmm.

31
00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.760
It's blocked off here, too!

32
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.190
Damn it, we just keep losing ground!

33
00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.030
I don't wanna die like this!

34
00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.270
Do you think all
those old guys got away safe?

35
00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:29.230
Who cares about them?

36
00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.570
We're in trouble!

37
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.110
Crap! I can't tell. Where are we?

38
00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.150
Who said you two
brats were allowed to escape?

39
00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.720
Bluejam!

40
00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:44.780
How come you're still here?

41
00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.310
I thought you were escaping
after the fire got lit!

42
00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.480
Did something happen?

43
00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.220
Shut up, ya punk!

44
00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.220
It's hopeless.

45
00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.360
You do know that, right?

46
00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.130
There's a sort of irony to this.

47
00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:00.200
It's a new perspective.

48
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.460
Humans are strange
creatures.

49
00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.660
I hit rock bottom and all
I can do is laugh about it.

50
00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.600
They're acting really weird.

51
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.790
It's creepy.

52
00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.940
Luffy! Run for it!

53
00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.910
Grab 'em!

54
00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.730
Where do you think you're going?

55
00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.270
We did this job together.

56
00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.400
That means we get to die together!

57
00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.770
We're not gonna die with you losers!

58
00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.770
We don't give up that easy!

59
00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.340
Is that so?

60
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.150
Actually, you still haven't told me
where you're hiding that treasure.

61
00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.170
Friends don't keep
secrets from each other.

62
00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:49.040
I'll save it for you before
the fire reaches it.

63
00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.770
All you have to do
is tell me where it is.

64
00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:54.900
Your life is in danger and
all you care about is treasure?

65
00:05:54.900 --> 00:06:01.050
Well, if you don't want it, then
you might as well tell me, right?

66
00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.470
Dammit, you've gone nuts.

67
00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:06.200
I'm just trying
to stop another tragedy.

68
00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.830
I already saw my ship
reduced to charcoal.

69
00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.540
It'd be a shame if that
happened to your treasure, too.

70
00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.170
All your hard work, and for nothing.

71
00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:17.440
You suck! Get your own treasure!

72
00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.340
All right. You win.

73
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.450
No!

74
00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:22.850
You spent forever collecting that!

75
00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.170
What would Sabo think?

76
00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:25.070
Shut up!

77
00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:26.340
Sabo would understand!

78
00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:30.010
The treasure isn't important anymore.

79
00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:33.070
The only thing that matters
is getting out of here alive.

80
00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:51.100
Six years.

81
00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.870
We've collected treasure for six
years and hid it in this tree.

82
00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.310
Why, thank you.

83
00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.210
Don't cry!

84
00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:01.150
It's okay, Luffy.
This won't be the end.

85
00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.510
What are you doing?

86
00:07:08.510 --> 00:07:10.480
I told you where it is, now let us go!

87
00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.150
I'm sorry. I don't think I trust you.

88
00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.350
Now then, about that treasure.

89
00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:18.120
Let's go. You can lead.

90
00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.120
You moron!

91
00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.020
That won't leave us time to escape,
and I'm not dying here! Just go!

92
00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.820
You've got the damn map!

93
00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.090
Listen, kid.

94
00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:32.170
Don't you dare piss me off.

95
00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:35.040
I'm not above stealing from
children, or murdering them.

96
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.540
I'll have my revenge.

97
00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:40.720
And believe me, those nobles will
regret the day they crossed Bluejam.

98
00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.070
And to think, you call
one of them your brother.

99
00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.070
They act like a little
money and influence

100
00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.740
makes them a gift to
the rest of the world,

101
00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:52.110
like it gives them the right
to look down on us like we're trash!

102
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.720
Shut up! Sabo isn't
like that! Take it back!

103
00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:57.790
Yes, he is! Face it!

104
00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:03.190
Sure, you stayed together, but he was
looking down on you the whole time!

105
00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.630
Liar!

106
00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:06.310
His parents are loaded.

107
00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:09.540
He doesn't have any of the problems
that you or I deal with!

108
00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:12.610
He used you idiots to get some kicks.

109
00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.620
He was just bored.
Then got a taste of real life

110
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.590
and he ran back home to his rich daddy!

111
00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:20.250
That's enough! Sabo is our brother!

112
00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.060
He's right! Sabo just wants to be free!

113
00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:27.860
Luffy!

114
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.770
Say goodbye, kid!

115
00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:39.340
Just let me go!

116
00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.980
Get the hell away from Luffy!

117
00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:16.480
Hey! Talk to me!

118
00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.220
What the hell did you do?

119
00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.150
Ow.

120
00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.210
You screwed up big time, brat!

121
00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.350
Go on.

122
00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.980
Try that crap again before I kill you.

123
00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.250
Get off of me, you scumbag!

124
00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.650
Time's up!

125
00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:38.420
Ace! No!

126
00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:41.020
Don't do it!

127
00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.590
Don't you dare hurt my boys!

128
00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.130
I'm not afraid to kill you!

129
00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.780
Thanks, but what are
you guys doing here?

130
00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.610
We aren't too late, are we?

131
00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.850
Yikes, you got roughed
up pretty bad, Luffy.

132
00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:23.920
You okay?

133
00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:25.550
I'll make it.

134
00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.920
And what about Sabo? I don't see him.

135
00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.490
He's safe in High Town.
He isn't with us anymore.

136
00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.320
Easy, now.

137
00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.660
I know you.

138
00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.990
You're that bandit
gorilla from Mount Corvo.

139
00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.490
Bandit, yes, gorilla, no.

140
00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:47.230
But that's not the point here.

141
00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:51.300
The point is, like it or not,
these kids are my responsibility.

142
00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:57.850
All right, then. Let's dance.

143
00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.690
Now! Everybody run!

144
00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.490
Roger, Boss!

145
00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:09.260
Hurry up! What're you doin'?

146
00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.960
Ace, we gotta get going!

147
00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:13.420
What's the matter?

148
00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:14.820
I'm staying.

149
00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.550
I won't run!

150
00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.950
You've got nothing to gain
here, you little idiot!

151
00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.020
Look, this place is on fire!

152
00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.820
Also, Bluejam is a hardened criminal!

153
00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:31.360
A little kid like you shouldn't
be fighting him to the death!

154
00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:34.830
- I-I gotta help Ace!
- Luffy, cut it out!

155
00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.300
Dammit! Stop!

156
00:11:38.430 --> 00:11:42.620
Take Luffy and get your
butts back to the hideout.

157
00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:43.730
What about you?

158
00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:47.650
I'll take care of Ace, no matter
how many asses I gotta kick!

159
00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.390
You're so cool.

160
00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.260
Now, go!

161
00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:55.090
Yes, ma'am!

162
00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:56.420
Ace!

163
00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.060
Come home safe, Boss!

164
00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:00.090
We'll be waiting for you!

165
00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:06.900
Look at that, how brave.

166
00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:12.160
But at the end of the day, you're just
a woman and a child against a pirate.

167
00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.690
Do you like those odds?

168
00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:19.110
Only two kinds of people survive in
battle: the strong and the cowardly.

169
00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.770
Bravery doesn't enter
the picture, I'm afraid.

170
00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.040
Oh, is that so?

171
00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.500
Hmm. Have it your way.

172
00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.990
We're all dead!

173
00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.330
Look around you!

174
00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:44.330
There's no way out now!

175
00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.200
Everything was fine! How
could this happen so quickly?

176
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:49.370
I'm burning! I'm burning!

177
00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.370
You and everyone else!

178
00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.250
Just let me die already.

179
00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.860
What the heck was that?

180
00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.520
Hey! It made a path through the fire!

181
00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.660
Whoa, did somebody do that on purpose?

182
00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:32.400
Who cares! Now we
can get out of this hellhole!

183
00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.430
Hey! Look you guys!

184
00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:38.160
There's a ship here! It's
waiting down by the shore!

185
00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.630
I dunno who and I don't know how,
but I think they're here to save us! Let's go!

186
00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:47.000
Hurry, before the fire comes back!

187
00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:53.180
I've seen nobles do some dreadful
things, but this takes the cake.

188
00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.790
Absolutely reprehensible!

189
00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.630
Anyhoo, this locale is
rather out of the way.

190
00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.430
How did you hear the news?

191
00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.000
Were you keeping
an eye on this country?

192
00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.400
Or perhaps, is there something
here of interest to you?

193
00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:10.970
What's happening here will happen in
the rest of the world soon enough.

194
00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:13.700
Human beings can't be thrown away.

195
00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.870
A world that allows that must change.

196
00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.480
No matter how long it takes, I will
stomp out this misery and injustice.

197
00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:27.420
I can't stay here, 'cause if
I do, then I'll never be free!

198
00:14:28.610 --> 00:14:33.450
The children born in this country must
have a future that they can believe in.

199
00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:49.430
If it's freedom you want, so long as
you have the will to fight for it,

200
00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.800
you are welcome aboard this ship!

201
00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.860
<b>Goa Kingdom "Royal Palace"</b>

202
00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:07.490
Are you sure that wall will protect us?

203
00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:10.260
Seems like the fire could
spread here any second.

204
00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.460
It won't last long.

205
00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:17.300
Surely, they'll let us into
High Town till it passes.

206
00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:18.530
Not a chance.

207
00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:23.200
Those gates are so tight,
even a flea can't get through.

208
00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:30.040
Let me go!

209
00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.150
Come back, Boss!

210
00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:34.410
– Ace, too!
– Ace, too!

211
00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.920
No! You can't die!

212
00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:43.990
No matter how their friends cried,
Ace and Dadan did not emerge from the flames

213
00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:46.430
consuming Gray Terminal.

214
00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:52.560
Easy, kiddo.

215
00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:55.300
You're still hurt, what're you doin'?

216
00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.200
What do ya think?
I'm looking for Ace and Dadan!

217
00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.340
That's not gonna work!

218
00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:06.570
I'm worried, too, but for right
now, we just have to wait.

219
00:16:06.570 --> 00:16:09.270
The military is down in Gray Terminal.

220
00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:13.910
Word is, they were sent in to clean up
everything after the fire died down.

221
00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:18.180
And by "clean up," I mean "take
care of any remaining evidence."

222
00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:21.690
I'm sure that extends to
killing off the survivors, too.

223
00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.060
You'd be no exception.

224
00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:25.490
But, Ace!

225
00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:47.650
<b>The remains of the Gray Terminal</b>

226
00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.020
Huh. Orders say to shoot any
survivors we find on sight.

227
00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:56.890
Yeah? What survivors?

228
00:16:56.890 --> 00:16:58.060
It's weird, though.

229
00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.160
I've hardly seen any corpses.

230
00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.630
That fire was pretty intense.

231
00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:04.170
Probably burned up their bones, too.

232
00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:08.530
I was up all night, scared that
fire would get over the wall.

233
00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:11.370
Shoulda known they wouldn't
burn decent people like us.

234
00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:14.310
I heard Bluejam's ship
wasn't quite so lucky.

235
00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:15.440
Good!

236
00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.410
Let's hope the bastard
was on it when it burned.

237
00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.830
Can't you see it will
always end this way, Sabo?

238
00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:30.360
The police and military
have photos of you.

239
00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.300
Try all you want. There's no escape!

240
00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:36.200
You'll never get out of High
Town, let alone this house,

241
00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.290
unless I expressly permit it.

242
00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:41.430
I need you on guard duty.

243
00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:44.250
Now, I'll look into
getting you new uniforms.

244
00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.320
I'm sorry sir, but
we have other duties.

245
00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:50.840
I'm a nobleman. That means
I get what I want.

246
00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.630
Don't worry, I'll have
a word with your superiors.

247
00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:55.030
Yes, sir.

248
00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:00.300
Listen, Sabo.
It's not too late for you.

249
00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:04.190
From now on, you'll lock yourself in
your room and learn to be a proper noble.

250
00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:04.930
No!

251
00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.630
I don't want to be cruel,

252
00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:11.020
but I am certainly capable of it
and anything else I so desire.

253
00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:14.000
You could disappear,
just like your friends.

254
00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.240
Are we clear?

255
00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:20.240
I think so.

256
00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:26.180
Ace. Luffy.

257
00:18:30.780 --> 00:18:33.680
If Stelly can
study hard, then so can you.

258
00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:35.820
Everything will work out fine.

259
00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.680
And then your parents, who worked so
hard to build a proper future for you,

260
00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.010
can finally be happy.

261
00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.580
Won't that be nice?

262
00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:48.360
I'm sure it'll be nice for you as well.

263
00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.960
Just give it some time.

264
00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:53.880
Papa!

265
00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.750
If you're sad, I can help!

266
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.020
Dependable as always, Stelly!

267
00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:05.630
We've got that big ceremony
coming up, you know.

268
00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:07.430
Let's buy you some new clothes.

269
00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:08.330
Heh.

270
00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.380
You'll look so handsome
for the Celestial Dragon!

271
00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:23.700
Study hard and I'll check
your homework tomorrow.

272
00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:26.070
Have a pleasant afternoon!

273
00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:38.280
Don't worry, guys. I'm fine.

274
00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:43.050
And you're tough,
so I know you're okay, too.

275
00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.990
There's no way you died in that fire.

276
00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.380
I just wish I could see you, even once.

277
00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:05.520
But if people follow me,
they'll find out you're still alive

278
00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.020
and you'll be in danger again.

279
00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:13.800
It looks nice from the outside,
but this house is a birdcage.

280
00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:17.830
I'm gonna lose my mind if I have
to stay in this stuffy, stuck-up place.

281
00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:28.080
I thought I found freedom,
but it seems to keep slipping away.

282
00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:34.580
All right! We're off.

283
00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.980
Take good care of Sabo.
We won't be back until late.

284
00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:39.980
Yes, sir. As you wish.

285
00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.010
After much anticipation,

286
00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:06.360
the day of the World Noble's visit
to the Goa Kingdom arrives at last.

287
00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:11.480
A lavish ceremony is prepared to greet
his ship as it enters the harbor.

288
00:21:16.730 --> 00:21:18.800
Hey, wait!

289
00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:21.000
Is that... a ship leaving port?

290
00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:22.740
A what?

291
00:21:22.740 --> 00:21:24.310
A fishing boat?

292
00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:28.410
Hey! Come back!

293
00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:30.610
You're blocking their path!

294
00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.320
Why, it's just a child!

295
00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.590
A little boy is steering that boat.

296
00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:37.490
Then, h-he's a noble?

297
00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.790
But surely all the families
are here watching!

298
00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:41.260
It can't be.

299
00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:45.250
Nice weather today!

300
00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:48.090
It's just perfect for setting sail!

301
00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.930
Crap! That's mine! It was stolen!

302
00:21:55.930 --> 00:21:58.270
I have nothing to do with this mess!

303
00:21:58.270 --> 00:22:01.170
His flag! He's got a jolly roger on it!

304
00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:03.970
Is he trying to be
a pirate or something?

305
00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:07.140
Does it matter? The kid's
flag isn't the issue here!

306
00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:09.100
He's heading straight for the ship.

307
00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:11.310
The Celestial Dragon
isn't gonna like this.

308
00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:16.140
Either you lose that boat, or you lose
your job, do you hear me? Fix it, now!

309
00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:17.480
Uh, yes, sir!

310
00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:19.970
Hey!

311
00:22:19.970 --> 00:22:23.500
Get back here, kid! Are you nuts?!

312
00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:28.010
I'm not afraid of anything
as long as I'm free.

313
00:22:28.010 --> 00:22:30.640
I just have to be far away from here.

314
00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:33.010
I have to follow my own dream.

315
00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:38.920
Nobody's gonna change me.

316
00:22:40.920 --> 00:22:45.990
Huh? Holy crap, Sabo, what do
ya think you're doin' out there?

317
00:22:47.690 --> 00:22:50.930
Give them a warm welcome, everyone!

318
00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:12.100
Wow, that's one big ship!

319
00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:14.530
It could run right over me, easy.

320
00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.740
Let's avoid that, shall we?

321
00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:23.410
This is a first for me!

322
00:23:23.410 --> 00:23:26.210
The Celestial Dragons hardly
ever make visits like this!

323
00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:28.210
I hope nobody mucks this up!

324
00:23:28.210 --> 00:23:30.710
We didn't burn all
those people for nothing!

325
00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:33.980
By the way, what is
that wretched little thing?

326
00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:37.690
Hm. It seems to be a fishing boat, sir.

327
00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.290
That's so cool.

328
00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:46.010
I hope I'm the captain of
a big ship like that someday.

329
00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:06.270
Easy, Luffy, easy!

330
00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:09.270
I know how you feel,
but it's still too dangerous.

331
00:24:09.270 --> 00:24:13.310
You got banged up pretty bad,
and the place is crawling with soldiers!

332
00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:14.240
Who cares?

333
00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:16.460
Please calm down and listen to me!

334
00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:18.430
We get it.

335
00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:21.600
We're scared, too, but right
now we just need to have faith

336
00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:24.000
that the boss and Ace are still alive.

337
00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:27.340
Dogra went back to look
for 'em, so be patient!

338
00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:29.710
Understand?

339
00:24:29.710 --> 00:24:32.940
This is hard on everyone, okay?

340
00:24:36.050 --> 00:24:38.180
The fishing boat has been hit!

341
00:24:38.180 --> 00:24:39.520
What happened to the child?

342
00:24:39.520 --> 00:24:42.590
That kid shouldn't have gotten
in the Celestial Dragon's way!

343
00:24:42.590 --> 00:24:43.990
Get outta there!

344
00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:46.820
Damn!

345
00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:50.250
Why'd he shoot at me?

346
00:24:50.250 --> 00:24:52.980
Saint Jalmack!
Th-There's a child on that ship!

347
00:24:52.980 --> 00:24:55.820
Anyone who flies a
black flag is a filthy pirate!

348
00:24:55.820 --> 00:24:57.820
His age is irrelevant.

349
00:24:57.820 --> 00:24:59.260
He must pay.

350
00:25:04.560 --> 00:25:05.630
Come on!

351
00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:07.600
A commoner should know better.

352
00:25:07.600 --> 00:25:11.130
Don't cross my ship,
you stupid pirate brat!

353
00:25:23.640 --> 00:25:26.040
What? Why would they fire
on that ship a second time?

354
00:25:26.040 --> 00:25:28.710
Who cares! We don't want to make
the Celestial Dragon mad!

355
00:25:28.710 --> 00:25:32.080
This is an important ceremony,
let him do whatever he wants!

356
00:25:32.080 --> 00:25:34.820
Ugh! Clear the wreckage already!

357
00:25:56.880 --> 00:25:58.340
Hey!

358
00:25:58.340 --> 00:25:59.840
I-I got news.

359
00:25:59.840 --> 00:26:00.880
Ace and the boss are...

360
00:26:00.880 --> 00:26:03.350
- What is it?

361
00:26:03.350 --> 00:26:05.480
They came back! They both made it!

362
00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:31.600
I was... so scared.

363
00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:33.200
She's badly wounded!

364
00:26:33.200 --> 00:26:36.280
Get them both inside, now! Hurry!

365
00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:37.310
Hang in there, Boss.

366
00:26:40.350 --> 00:26:41.950
- Ace!

367
00:26:41.950 --> 00:26:42.920
Get off!

368
00:26:45.310 --> 00:26:48.620
C'mon. Did you seriously
think I was dead?

369
00:26:48.620 --> 00:26:49.380
Maybe!

370
00:26:49.380 --> 00:26:50.520
Quit crying already!

371
00:26:52.190 --> 00:26:54.360
I'm standing right
in front of ya, dummy!

372
00:26:54.360 --> 00:26:57.760
C'mon, Ace! Take it easy
on the kiddo for once.

373
00:26:57.760 --> 00:27:00.060
Luffy's just happy to see you.

374
00:27:06.000 --> 00:27:07.670
What happened the night of the fire?

375
00:27:07.670 --> 00:27:10.970
We all came back here with Luffy,
so we haven't heard a word.

376
00:27:10.970 --> 00:27:13.510
Can you tell us everything that
happened to you and the boss?

377
00:27:14.960 --> 00:27:15.660
Oh.

378
00:27:15.660 --> 00:27:18.530
Well, um, we fought Bluejam.

379
00:27:20.440 --> 00:27:22.510
We barely defeated him.

380
00:27:25.910 --> 00:27:27.650
And we tried to catch up to you guys

381
00:27:27.650 --> 00:27:31.950
as fast as we could, but the
fire was blocking our way.

382
00:27:32.210 --> 00:27:34.150
We made it through the fire.

383
00:27:34.150 --> 00:27:37.490
Dadan was suffering from
some serious burns, though.

384
00:27:37.490 --> 00:27:41.350
Eventually we managed to get to the
riverside in the In-Between Forest.

385
00:27:45.430 --> 00:27:49.530
I went into town to steal medicine
and grab whatever food I could find.

386
00:27:49.530 --> 00:27:53.530
I'm no doctor, but I did what
I could to save Dadan's life.

387
00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:01.850
What an ordeal!

388
00:28:01.850 --> 00:28:05.080
In any case, all that matters is
that both of you are back safe!

389
00:28:05.080 --> 00:28:08.220
I'm sorry. I made you worry.

390
00:28:08.220 --> 00:28:11.560
That fire was huge and they
were hunting down survivors.

391
00:28:11.560 --> 00:28:13.890
Sabo must think we're dead right now.

392
00:28:17.750 --> 00:28:22.040
This kingdom's likely full of lowly
plebeians that will get in my way.

393
00:28:22.040 --> 00:28:23.940
Be on the lookout for any disruption.

394
00:28:23.940 --> 00:28:25.240
Right!

395
00:28:30.350 --> 00:28:32.620
I wonder what Sabo's been up to.

396
00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:35.170
But at least Ace finally
made it back, right?

397
00:28:35.170 --> 00:28:37.140
He even carried Dadan home with him.

398
00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:41.280
Ace, when I came for you...

399
00:28:42.240 --> 00:28:43.110
I'm staying.

400
00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:45.150
I won't run!

401
00:28:46.110 --> 00:28:48.450
Why did you do that?

402
00:28:48.450 --> 00:28:49.510
I don't know.

403
00:28:49.510 --> 00:28:51.640
I can't help but get fired up.

404
00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:58.080
I'm afraid if I run, that I might leave
something important behind me, so I fight.

405
00:28:59.820 --> 00:29:03.150
Luffy was there, so I had no choice.

406
00:29:04.220 --> 00:29:07.160
It's tough to explain,
but I think that's why.

407
00:29:10.300 --> 00:29:14.610
Even when he faced a wave
of far more powerful enemies,

408
00:29:14.610 --> 00:29:17.010
Roger would never
think of running away.

409
00:29:17.010 --> 00:29:20.180
Did that fool have a death wish?
Running away's a strategy, too.

410
00:29:20.180 --> 00:29:23.550
For him it wasn't even
an option. Think about it.

411
00:29:23.550 --> 00:29:25.810
Retreat means leaving people behind.

412
00:29:25.810 --> 00:29:29.890
If Roger ran he'd be abandoning
his crew, the people he loved most.

413
00:29:29.890 --> 00:29:33.410
So, when you think about it,
it's not that he "wouldn't run,"

414
00:29:33.410 --> 00:29:36.920
rather, he made sure the enemy
couldn't go after his crew.

415
00:29:36.920 --> 00:29:38.570
He always protected them.

416
00:29:38.570 --> 00:29:41.440
He was a different kind of
animal in times like those.

417
00:29:41.440 --> 00:29:43.550
He once wrecked a whole country's army

418
00:29:43.550 --> 00:29:46.880
'cause some soldiers decided
to mouth off about his men.

419
00:29:46.880 --> 00:29:49.490
When he was angry,
Roger would get violent.

420
00:29:49.490 --> 00:29:53.830
He was selfish and short-tempered,
but he wore his heart on his sleeve.

421
00:29:53.830 --> 00:29:56.260
He was like a boy that never grew up.

422
00:29:56.260 --> 00:29:59.960
For better or worse, his
childhood was a lot like Ace's.

423
00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:04.240
The pain he went through just made him
hold on tighter to the ones he loved.

424
00:30:07.690 --> 00:30:12.480
Roger could be a very reckless man,
but he lived to become King of the Pirates.

425
00:30:12.480 --> 00:30:14.320
No easy feat.

426
00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:19.590
Despite his flaws and his bad reputation,
his crew still trusted him completely.

427
00:30:19.590 --> 00:30:25.360
Sure, I may be a Marine,
but even I can't help respecting him.

428
00:30:25.360 --> 00:30:27.710
That's why I decided
to take care of Ace.

429
00:30:27.710 --> 00:30:31.250
I'm the one
taking care of him, you ass!

430
00:30:31.250 --> 00:30:33.820
Do you got somethin'
you wanna say to me?

431
00:30:33.820 --> 00:30:36.320
No, never mind.

432
00:30:36.320 --> 00:30:39.060
People all over
the world still hate Roger,

433
00:30:39.060 --> 00:30:42.190
and even though Ace holds
a grudge against him, too,

434
00:30:42.190 --> 00:30:45.230
they really are
"like father, like son."

435
00:30:45.230 --> 00:30:49.240
All right! Wonder who's gonna win!

436
00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:50.870
Dogra!

437
00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:54.540
You went to town to look
for Ace and Dadan, right?

438
00:30:54.540 --> 00:30:56.510
Surprise, they came back home already!

439
00:30:56.510 --> 00:30:58.580
Oh. Did they really?

440
00:30:58.580 --> 00:31:01.520
That's just great. Perfect.

441
00:31:01.520 --> 00:31:03.740
What? Sabo?

442
00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:04.810
That can't be.

443
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:07.850
You're lying to me, dammit!

444
00:31:07.850 --> 00:31:09.760
Why would you even joke
about that kind of thing?

445
00:31:09.760 --> 00:31:11.110
Take it easy!

446
00:31:11.110 --> 00:31:13.650
I told you exactly what I saw, I swear!

447
00:31:13.650 --> 00:31:14.880
I know how you feel.

448
00:31:14.880 --> 00:31:17.720
Everything happened so fast
I could hardly believe it!

449
00:31:17.720 --> 00:31:20.980
It felt like a nightmare,
but I know that was Sabo.

450
00:31:20.980 --> 00:31:22.290
Shut up!

451
00:31:22.290 --> 00:31:24.460
We watched him go back with his
dad to their home in High Town!

452
00:31:24.460 --> 00:31:26.720
You can't have seen him
out at sea by himself!

453
00:31:26.720 --> 00:31:28.780
That's right! Sabo is with his family!

454
00:31:28.780 --> 00:31:31.110
Bandits like us know how he feels!

455
00:31:31.110 --> 00:31:35.510
We know what it means to be turned
away from your home, to be free!

456
00:31:35.510 --> 00:31:37.810
Sabo didn't wanna be a noble!

457
00:31:37.810 --> 00:31:41.250
If he was truly happy, he
wouldn't have gone out to sea!

458
00:31:41.250 --> 00:31:45.020
And the Sabo I saw wasn't just
sailing away from his family,

459
00:31:45.020 --> 00:31:47.080
he was flying a jolly roger!

460
00:31:58.870 --> 00:32:01.770
We shouldn't've have
let him go! It's all our fault!

461
00:32:03.110 --> 00:32:06.010
Even if I had parents,
I was still alone.

462
00:32:06.880 --> 00:32:08.040
Sabo!

463
00:32:08.040 --> 00:32:10.610
Why didn't we go into town
and bring him back here?

464
00:32:10.610 --> 00:32:12.210
We're so stupid!

465
00:32:12.210 --> 00:32:14.550
Tell me where I can find
the bastard that killed him!

466
00:32:14.550 --> 00:32:16.380
I'm gonna beat him
to death with my bare hands!

467
00:32:16.380 --> 00:32:18.920
You can't kill a Celestial
Dragon, that's impossible!

468
00:32:18.920 --> 00:32:21.190
I'll make him pay!

469
00:32:21.190 --> 00:32:22.320
Hold on, Ace!

470
00:32:23.860 --> 00:32:26.030
Enough of that, you little punk!

471
00:32:27.480 --> 00:32:28.820
Get off!

472
00:32:28.820 --> 00:32:33.140
You think you're so tough, when you're
really just a cocky, stubborn little brat!

473
00:32:33.140 --> 00:32:35.110
What can you do against a World Noble?

474
00:32:35.110 --> 00:32:37.010
You think he's just some thug?

475
00:32:37.010 --> 00:32:38.810
You're just some no-name kid!

476
00:32:38.810 --> 00:32:40.650
You'll die and nobody will give a crap!

477
00:32:40.650 --> 00:32:43.020
Swept under the rug the very next day!

478
00:32:43.020 --> 00:32:45.690
It was this whole rotten
country that killed Sabo.

479
00:32:45.690 --> 00:32:47.490
This rotten world!

480
00:32:47.490 --> 00:32:49.890
What can a scrawny brat
like you do about it?

481
00:32:51.190 --> 00:32:54.230
Your father on the other hand
changed the world with his death!

482
00:32:54.230 --> 00:32:59.270
When you become a man as important as him,
then and only then, can you take revenge!

483
00:33:02.790 --> 00:33:04.590
Tie this fool up!

484
00:33:04.590 --> 00:33:07.230
Uh, yes, ma'am!

485
00:33:07.230 --> 00:33:10.800
Sabo!

486
00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:12.300
Dammit!

487
00:33:14.240 --> 00:33:15.440
Shut up, Luffy!

488
00:33:15.440 --> 00:33:18.020
Quit crying like a girl,
or else I'll... I'll...

489
00:33:34.770 --> 00:33:37.870
You've come to your senses now, I hope.

490
00:33:41.470 --> 00:33:42.910
Guys, untie him.

491
00:33:42.910 --> 00:33:43.810
– Right.
– Right.

492
00:33:43.810 --> 00:33:45.410
- Huh?

493
00:33:45.410 --> 00:33:46.940
Try to keep your cool, okay?

494
00:33:46.940 --> 00:33:48.010
Where's Luffy?

495
00:33:48.010 --> 00:33:50.780
He was crying all night.
Finally fell asleep.

496
00:33:52.010 --> 00:33:54.780
Oh, my gosh! You're not
gonna believe this!

497
00:33:54.780 --> 00:33:56.240
- Huh?
- We got a letter!

498
00:33:56.240 --> 00:33:57.610
It's from Sabo!

499
00:33:57.610 --> 00:33:59.450
He must have sent it before he left!

500
00:33:59.450 --> 00:34:00.950
Look, I think it's really from him!

501
00:34:00.950 --> 00:34:03.380
Give it.

502
00:34:03.380 --> 00:34:05.220
Don't worry, I won't head to town.

503
00:34:05.220 --> 00:34:07.620
It's for Luffy and me, isn't it?

504
00:34:13.900 --> 00:34:18.100
Ace, Luffy, I hope you
guys weren't hurt in the fire.

505
00:34:18.100 --> 00:34:22.040
I'm worried about you both, but
something tells me you're okay.

506
00:34:22.040 --> 00:34:24.040
I've got a surprise to tell you.

507
00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:28.410
By the time you get this
letter, I'll be long gone.

508
00:34:28.410 --> 00:34:31.580
That's right, I'm heading out to sea.

509
00:34:31.580 --> 00:34:35.650
One thing led to another,
and I decided to set out before you two.

510
00:34:40.900 --> 00:34:42.330
I don't know where I'm going yet,

511
00:34:42.330 --> 00:34:45.540
but I do know that anywhere
will be better than this place.

512
00:34:45.540 --> 00:34:48.430
And don't worry, I haven't
given up on my dream.

513
00:34:48.430 --> 00:34:50.900
I'm still gonna be a pirate!

514
00:34:50.900 --> 00:34:54.330
I got a head start, but I'm sure
you'll catch up in no time.

515
00:34:54.330 --> 00:34:57.700
When we meet again,
we'll be unstoppable!

516
00:34:58.940 --> 00:35:01.210
We'll have our
reunion on the Grand Line,

517
00:35:01.210 --> 00:35:04.550
three pirate captains,
more free than the wind!

518
00:35:06.380 --> 00:35:09.320
By the way, Ace, I'm curious.

519
00:35:09.320 --> 00:35:12.920
Which one of us do you think
is the real "big brother"?

520
00:35:12.920 --> 00:35:17.520
Anyway, wherever we sail, we'll
always have our brotherhood.

521
00:35:17.520 --> 00:35:22.320
It may sound kinda cheesy, but that bond
is what I treasure most in this world.

522
00:35:26.420 --> 00:35:29.560
Luffy is still weak and a crybaby.

523
00:35:29.560 --> 00:35:32.000
Who knows if he'll
ever grow out of that.

524
00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:41.300
But he's still our little brother,
so please take good care of him!
